WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.200
Our next guest has his comedy
special, "Nori,"

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.434
available now on Spotify.

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:08.434
Please welcome the very funny
Nore Davis.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:12.100
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.734
-Hey. What's up?

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.100
Thank you, thank you. Alright.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.367
Let's do this before it's
my bedtime 'cause I'm tired.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:22.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:24.234
When you in 30
and after 10:00 p.m.,

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.801
your body's in low-power mode.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:29.367
It's something like I grew
this janitor in me.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:30.767
He's like, "Oh, these lights
should be off."

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.667
"But wait, I'm driving."

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:35.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.300
"That's too much electricity,
young man.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.300
You should be in bed.
That is too much.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.868
Too much."

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.467
But only thing that really
keeps me up

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:45.367
is, like, I love watching
my movie franchise.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.067
"Jurassic Park,"
I love those films.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:49.234
[ Crowd cheers ]
Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.367
'Cause it really makes white
people believe dinosaurs

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.367
would've been their pets.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.834
They hit them with that
Chris Pratt palm,

00:00:56.834 --> 00:01:00.467
"hey, hey, hey,
hey, hey, hey, Blue.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.200
Hey, you know me."

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.567
"Hey, hey."

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.234
It's like reptiles don't listen.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.100
I've never seen a white person
walking a Komodo dragon.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.167
But it's like, "Hey, hey, hey,
hey. You know me."

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:17.234
And the raptor stops, like,
"Oh, you lucky

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.601
I love 'Parks and Recreation.'"

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:21.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.701
"You lucky. I'll see you later,
Star-Lord."

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.701
He comes back.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.667
Capitalism gonna cap, baby.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:34.000
But, like, how long are we going
to keep doing this hierarchy?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.234
Working class, poor,
rich, wealthy.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:39.868
It's like a game,
but it's our real lives.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.067
The wealthy and rich
are playing Monopoly.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.000
Working class and poor,
we're playing Trouble.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.667
Pop, pop! $6?

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:54.434
That's all I can do today.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:55.834
Pop, pop! Two?

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.334
I can't even leave the house.

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.934
I got to wait for a six.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.801
It's like the wealthy,
they have the money.

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.300
Just print the money.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.934
You have it.
Just, like, command P.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:12.467
It's always been that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:15.067
It never changed,
no matter how old you are.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.834
But, you know, I'm not
a politician.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.367
I'm just an Aries.
That's all I know.

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:24.367
I'm always trying to get rid of
generational trauma

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.601
within my family, you know,
because I'm a millennial,

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:28.934
and I was raised
by baby boomer parents.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:32.133
And you know that
we was their property.

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.634
You know that saying, "I brought
you in this world,

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.801
I'll take you out"?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.934
What makes you think
that's a good investment?

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:44.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:47.000
You can always tell millennials
have trauma from their parents

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.033
'cause when they talk to
their friends,

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:49.701
they call them
by their first name.

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:51.601
"Hey, how's your mom?"
"Who, Jackie?"

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:53.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:57.167
"She alright. Still judging."

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:02.467
They have so much trauma,
but I give them grace

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.467
because, you know, therapy just
came out in 2020.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:05.834
They missed it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:09.267
It just came out.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:11.133
It's so hard.

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:13.000
Like, you ever tell
a baby boomer you love them?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.100
"I love you."
They start malfunctioning.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.067
[ Laughter ]
"Love?"

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:20.400
It was my dad's birthday
the other day.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.567
I was like,
"Hey, Dad, happy birthday."

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.000
He was like, "Alright."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.300
"Alright"? Not even like
a cool "Alright!"

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.434
It was like a prisoner telling
the guard, like,

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:32.567
"Hey, happy birthday."
"Alright, alright.

00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:36.467
Back in your cell.
Back in there."

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.133
So that's why I always do,
like, an outward

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:41.634
love expression
towards my child.

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.334
Like, he's generation alpha.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.067
And, you know, so with
a millennial,

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:46.601
they are not our property.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.767
They are content.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.934
That's right. "Get to work!"

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.767
"Dad, I'm hungry."
"You go viral, you eat!"

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.934
"When you go viral, you'll eat.
Come on, let's go."

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:03.033
I'm Nore Davis.
Thank you so much!

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.734
-Hey, hey, hey.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:16.000
-Nore Davis.
"Nori" is available on Spotify.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.300
We'll be right back, everybody.

